1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:01,683
Day one.

2
00:00:01,683 --> 00:00:03,355
You're a waiter
on a cruise ship.

3
00:00:03,355 --> 00:00:04,911
Three thousand
passengers.

4
00:00:04,911 --> 00:00:06,919
Seven days at sea.

5
00:00:07,669 --> 00:00:08,900
Then every
phone on board

6
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:09,759
buzzes at once.

7
00:00:09,759 --> 00:00:11,663
Stay in
your cabins.

8
00:00:12,013 --> 00:00:13,743
Ladies and gentlemen,
this is

9
00:00:13,743 --> 00:00:14,857
your captain.

10
00:00:14,857 --> 00:00:16,947
Please return
to your cabins.

11
00:00:16,947 --> 00:00:18,468
We are changing
course to the

12
00:00:18,468 --> 00:00:19,861
nearest—

13
00:00:21,211 --> 00:00:23,359
And the captain
stops talking...

14
00:00:23,359 --> 00:00:25,065
mid-sentence.

15
00:00:26,515 --> 00:00:27,618
On Deck Five,
people are

16
00:00:27,618 --> 00:00:29,777
walking strangely.
Too slowly.

17
00:00:29,777 --> 00:00:31,948
And they're
coming this way.

18
00:00:33,498 --> 00:00:35,019
You learn the
most important

19
00:00:35,019 --> 00:00:36,470
thing on this
ship in the next

20
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:38,188
ten seconds.

21
00:00:40,538 --> 00:00:41,989
They don't
see you.

22
00:00:41,989 --> 00:00:43,742
They hear you.

23
00:00:46,292 --> 00:00:47,592
Rule number one.

24
00:00:47,592 --> 00:00:48,916
Don't run to
the lifeboats.

25
00:00:48,916 --> 00:00:50,750
Everyone
else will.

26
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:53,215
You go down.

27
00:00:53,215 --> 00:00:54,654
To the one place
nobody thinks

28
00:00:54,654 --> 00:00:56,883
about. The galley.

29
00:00:57,733 --> 00:00:58,917
Food for
three weeks.

30
00:00:58,917 --> 00:01:00,299
Water for
nine days.

31
00:01:00,299 --> 00:01:01,880
And one
steel door.

32
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:03,238
You push a cart
against the

33
00:01:03,238 --> 00:01:05,688
door...
and you wait.

34
00:01:11,038 --> 00:01:12,536
Rule number two.
Be quiet.

35
00:01:12,536 --> 00:01:14,335
They follow sound.

36
00:01:14,985 --> 00:01:16,912
That night,
the engines stop.

37
00:01:16,912 --> 00:01:18,236
The lights
stay on.

38
00:01:18,236 --> 00:01:20,325
Nobody tells
you why.

39
00:01:21,775 --> 00:01:22,564
Day three.

40
00:01:22,564 --> 00:01:24,436
You learn the
ship's new rhythm.

41
00:01:24,436 --> 00:01:26,537
Footsteps above
you at noon.

42
00:01:26,537 --> 00:01:28,407
Something dragging
at midnight.

43
00:01:28,407 --> 00:01:30,183
And long,
long silences in

44
00:01:30,183 --> 00:01:31,634
between.

45
00:01:32,684 --> 00:01:33,381
Day five.

46
00:01:33,381 --> 00:01:35,252
Someone has been
in the cold room.

47
00:01:35,252 --> 00:01:36,819
Half your
bread is gone.

48
00:01:36,819 --> 00:01:38,178
And the infected
don't close

49
00:01:38,178 --> 00:01:39,942
doors behind them.

50
00:01:41,192 --> 00:01:42,179
Day seven.

51
00:01:42,179 --> 00:01:43,293
You wait in
the dark to see

52
00:01:43,293 --> 00:01:45,232
who's stealing
your food.

53
00:01:55,882 --> 00:01:57,287
Whoever it is...

54
00:01:57,287 --> 00:01:58,471
knows this ship
better than

55
00:01:58,471 --> 00:01:59,876
you do.

56
00:02:01,326 --> 00:02:02,034
Day nine.

57
00:02:02,034 --> 00:02:03,662
The last bottle
of water.

58
00:02:03,662 --> 00:02:04,986
The nearest
water is the ice

59
00:02:04,986 --> 00:02:06,495
machine in
the crew mess.

60
00:02:06,495 --> 00:02:09,095
Forty steps down
a dark corridor.

61
00:02:16,845 --> 00:02:18,180
Unfortunately,
the ice machine

62
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:19,039
is the loudest
thing on this

63
00:02:19,039 --> 00:02:20,328
ship.

64
00:02:24,378 --> 00:02:25,597
This is the
Coast Guard on

65
00:02:25,597 --> 00:02:26,897
channel sixteen.

66
00:02:26,897 --> 00:02:28,523
All ports
are closed.

67
00:02:28,523 --> 00:02:30,032
Any vessel
carrying infected

68
00:02:30,032 --> 00:02:31,205
will not be
allowed to reach

69
00:02:31,205 --> 00:02:34,130
the coast.
We will use force.

70
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,534
That night,
the speakers in

71
00:02:36,534 --> 00:02:38,577
the ceiling
click on.

72
00:02:41,327 --> 00:02:42,233
Nobody speaks.

73
00:02:42,233 --> 00:02:44,276
Someone is just...
listening.

74
00:02:44,276 --> 00:02:46,203
Then they
click off.

75
00:02:46,353 --> 00:02:47,618
Day twelve.

76
00:02:47,618 --> 00:02:49,267
Through the
porthole...

77
00:02:49,267 --> 00:02:51,763
a light.
A lighthouse.

78
00:02:51,763 --> 00:02:54,480
The ship has
drifted toward land.

79
00:02:56,130 --> 00:02:57,581
Then, deep
below you...

80
00:02:57,581 --> 00:02:59,566
the engines
start again.

81
00:03:01,416 --> 00:03:04,109
And the ship turns
away from land.

82
00:03:05,359 --> 00:03:06,648
Someone else is
alive on this

83
00:03:06,648 --> 00:03:07,333
ship.

84
00:03:07,333 --> 00:03:09,767
And they don't
want to be rescued.

85
00:03:09,767 --> 00:03:11,044
You could stay
in the galley.

86
00:03:11,044 --> 00:03:13,264
Safe. Fed.
And blind.

87
00:03:13,264 --> 00:03:14,425
Or you could
find out who's

88
00:03:14,425 --> 00:03:15,818
driving.

89
00:03:26,568 --> 00:03:29,168
Rule number two
works both ways.

90
00:03:30,418 --> 00:03:31,440
Don't move.

91
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:32,868
Hands where I
can see them.

92
00:03:32,868 --> 00:03:34,412
Both of them.

93
00:03:35,162 --> 00:03:36,927
Where did
you get that?

94
00:03:38,077 --> 00:03:39,192
You're the waiter.

95
00:03:39,192 --> 00:03:41,256
The one who hums
when he's scared.

96
00:03:41,256 --> 00:03:42,626
Turns out you
weren't as quiet

97
00:03:42,626 --> 00:03:43,892
as you thought.

98
00:03:43,892 --> 00:03:45,181
Day one,
the bridge ordered

99
00:03:45,181 --> 00:03:46,063
all stop.

100
00:03:46,063 --> 00:03:47,549
Then the line
went dead.

101
00:03:47,549 --> 00:03:49,672
Nobody's opened
that door since.

102
00:03:49,672 --> 00:03:50,996
Then the Coast
Guard started

103
00:03:50,996 --> 00:03:52,238
sinking ships.

104
00:03:52,238 --> 00:03:53,503
So every time
we drift too

105
00:03:53,503 --> 00:03:54,769
close to land...

106
00:03:54,769 --> 00:03:56,011
I start the
engines and take

107
00:03:56,011 --> 00:03:57,263
us back out.

108
00:03:57,263 --> 00:03:58,633
So that's
who's driving.

109
00:03:58,633 --> 00:03:59,469
Not a ghost.

110
00:03:59,469 --> 00:04:01,675
A very tired
engineer.

111
00:04:02,025 --> 00:04:03,697
Two survivors.
One kitchen.

112
00:04:03,697 --> 00:04:04,826
One engine room.

113
00:04:04,826 --> 00:04:06,161
She keeps the
ship alive.

114
00:04:06,161 --> 00:04:08,077
You keep her fed.

115
00:04:12,227 --> 00:04:13,376
Day twenty-nine.

116
00:04:13,376 --> 00:04:15,328
Fuel for one
more day.

117
00:04:15,328 --> 00:04:17,278
Tomorrow we pick
a direction.

118
00:04:17,278 --> 00:04:19,229
And we don't
come back.

119
00:04:23,179 --> 00:04:24,547
That's not me.

120
00:04:24,547 --> 00:04:25,766
Steering just
switched to the

121
00:04:25,766 --> 00:04:26,695
bridge.

122
00:04:26,695 --> 00:04:27,693
Nobody's been
up there in

123
00:04:27,693 --> 00:04:29,423
thirty days.

124
00:04:36,173 --> 00:04:37,032
Engine room.

125
00:04:37,032 --> 00:04:38,770
This is
the bridge.

126
00:04:38,770 --> 00:04:40,477
Thank you for
keeping us alive.

127
00:04:40,477 --> 00:04:42,299
I'll take it
from here.

128
00:04:43,049 --> 00:04:44,999
That's not
the captain.

129
00:04:46,749 --> 00:04:47,504
Thirty days.

130
00:04:47,504 --> 00:04:48,990
You survived the
outbreak, the

131
00:04:48,990 --> 00:04:50,625
hunger and
the sea.

132
00:04:50,625 --> 00:04:52,750
You found out
who was driving.

133
00:04:52,750 --> 00:04:54,038
Now you just
have to find out

134
00:04:54,038 --> 00:04:55,826
where he's
taking you.
